module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.SegreEmbedding.SegreClosedImmersion
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjChain.EventualSurjective
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjPolyChart.Away
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.SymmetricAlgebraGrading

/-!
# An algebra is a closed subscheme of the `Proj` of its symmetric algebra

Let `B` be an algebra over a commutative ring `R`. Sending a degree-one element `b` of
`Sym_R(B)` to `b · t` defines a homomorphism of graded rings `Sym_R(B) ⟶ B[t]`, which is
surjective in every positive degree — in degree `d ≥ 1` the element `b · tᵈ` is the image of
`b · 1^{d-1}` — and therefore induces a **closed immersion**
`Proj B[t] ⟶ Proj (Sym_R B)` by Tag 01N1.

This is the engine of [Stacks, Tag 0B3I] with the symmetric algebra in place of a polynomial
ring: the source chooses module generators of `B` over `R` to land in `𝐏ⁿ` and then has to
argue separately that the resulting immersion is closed, whereas the homomorphism below needs
no generators, no finiteness and no hypothesis on `R`, and is closed immediately.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.SymAlgebraProjImmersion.symLine`: the `R`-algebra homomorphism
  `Sym_R(B) ⟶ B[t]` sending `b` in degree one to `b · t`.
* `Stacks.SymAlgebraProjImmersion.symLineGradedHom`: the same map as a homomorphism of graded
  rings, `Sym_R(B) →+*ᵍ B[t]`.
* `Stacks.SymAlgebraProjImmersion.projLineHom`: the induced morphism
  `Proj B[t] ⟶ Proj (Sym_R B)`.
* `Stacks.SymAlgebraProjImmersion.awayEquiv`: the degree-zero homogeneous localization of `B[t]`
  at `t`, which is `B`.
* `Stacks.SymAlgebraProjImmersion.projIsoSpec`: the identification `Proj B[t] ≅ Spec B`.
* `Stacks.SymAlgebraProjImmersion.specToProjSym`: the resulting morphism
  `Spec B ⟶ Proj (Sym_R B)`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SymAlgebraProjImmersion.surjective_symLineGradedHom`: the degree-`d` component is
  surjective for `d ≥ 1`.
* `Stacks.SymAlgebraProjImmersion.isClosedImmersion_projLineHom`: **the induced morphism
  `Proj B[t] ⟶ Proj (Sym_R B)` is a closed immersion.**
* `Stacks.SymAlgebraProjImmersion.basicOpen_X_eq_top`: the standard open of `t` is all of
  `Proj B[t]`, because the irrelevant ideal of `B[t]` is generated by `t`.
* `Stacks.SymAlgebraProjImmersion.isClosedImmersion_specToProjSym`: **`Spec B` is a closed
  subscheme of `Proj (Sym_R B)`.**

## Implementation notes

`B[t]` is `MvPolynomial (Fin 1) B` with the total-degree grading
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjPolyChart.polyGrading B 0`, which is the grading the `Proj` API of
this repository is written against. Its degree-`d` part is the `B`-span of `t^d`, which is the
content of `Stacks.SymAlgebraProjImmersion.eq_C_mul_X_pow`: a polynomial in one variable
homogeneous of degree `d` is its `t^d`-coefficient times `t^d`.

Degree zero is excluded from surjectivity and must be: there the homomorphism is the structure
map `R ⟶ B`. So the hypothesis available is Tag 01N1's eventual surjectivity, not surjectivity,
and the closed immersion comes from
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SegreClosedImmersion.isClosedImmersion_mapHomOfTop` rather than from
`AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B3I](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B3I)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N1)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N0)

## Not done here

No project tag is attached, and nothing here is specific to a finite morphism. Tag 0B3I asserts
that a finite morphism of schemes is projective, and from the closed immersion below that needs
two further things.

* **Over the base.** `Stacks.SymAlgebraProjImmersion.specToProjSym` is not yet related to the
  structure morphisms over `Spec R`, which `AlgebraicGeometry.IsProjective` asks for. The
  identification of the degree-zero part is `SymmetricAlgebra.symmetricPowerZeroEquiv` and the
  compatibility of `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj.mapHomOfTop` with
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.toSpecZero` is `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj.mapHom_toSpecZero`
  read through `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj.topIso_inv_isoOfEq_hom_ι`.
* **Globalizing.** Over an affine base this and
  `Stacks.SymGraded.projectiveBundleIsoProjectiveSpaceOfModule` identify the target with the
  projective bundle of `B` viewed as a module. Over an arbitrary base the chart morphisms it
  produces over the affine opens of the base have to be glued into a single morphism to
  `Stacks.SymGraded.schemeProjectiveBundle`, and the mapping-in statement available,
  `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.exists_hom_relativeProjToBase`, is both existential and local on
  the base, so it cannot be glued.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory MvPolynomial
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjPolyChart
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjShared

namespace Stacks.SymAlgebraProjImmersion

universe u

attribute [local instance] MvPolynomial.gradedAlgebra
attribute [local instance_reducible] ProjectiveSpectrum.top

variable (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (B : Type u) [CommRing B] [Algebra R B]

/-! ### Homogeneous polynomials in one variable -/

/-- **A polynomial in one variable homogeneous of degree `d` is a multiple of `t^d`**, namely its
`t^d`-coefficient times `t^d`. -/
public theorem eq_C_mul_X_pow {d : ℕ} {y : MvPolynomial (Fin 1) B}
    (hy : y ∈ polyGrading B 0 d) :
    y = MvPolynomial.C (y.coeff (Finsupp.single 0 d)) * MvPolynomial.X (0 : Fin 1) ^ d := by
  have hhom : y.IsHomogeneous d := (MvPolynomial.mem_homogeneousSubmodule _ _).1 hy
  have hsingle : ∀ m : Fin 1 →₀ ℕ, m = Finsupp.single 0 (m 0) := fun m =>
    Finsupp.ext fun i => by
      rw [Subsingleton.elim i 0, Finsupp.single_eq_same]
  refine MvPolynomial.ext _ _ fun m => ?_
  rw [MvPolynomial.coeff_C_mul, MvPolynomial.coeff_X_pow]
  split_ifs with hm
  · rw [mul_one, hm]
  · rw [mul_zero]
    by_contra hne
    have hdeg : m.degree = d := by
      rw [Finsupp.degree_eq_weight_one]; exact hhom hne
    have hm0 : m 0 = d := by
      have hds : (Finsupp.single (0 : Fin 1) (m 0)).degree = d := by
        rw [← hsingle m]; exact hdeg
      rwa [Finsupp.degree_single] at hds
    exact hm (by rw [← hm0]; exact (hsingle m).symm)

/-! ### The graded homomorphism to the polynomial ring -/

/-- The `R`-linear map `B ⟶ B[t]` sending `b` to `b · t`. -/
public def lineCoord : B →ₗ[R] MvPolynomial (Fin 1) B where
  toFun b := MvPolynomial.C b * MvPolynomial.X (0 : Fin 1)
  map_add' b b' := by rw [map_add, add_mul]
  map_smul' r b := by
    have halg : (algebraMap R (MvPolynomial (Fin 1) B)) r =
        MvPolynomial.C (algebraMap R B r) := by
      rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply R B (MvPolynomial (Fin 1) B),
        MvPolynomial.algebraMap_eq]
    rw [RingHom.id_apply, Algebra.smul_def, Algebra.smul_def, halg, map_mul, mul_assoc]

/-- `lineCoord R B b` is `C b * X 0`. -/
@[simp] public theorem lineCoord_apply (b : B) :
    lineCoord R B b = MvPolynomial.C b * MvPolynomial.X (0 : Fin 1) := rfl

/-- **The homomorphism `Sym_R(B) ⟶ B[t]`** sending a degree-one element `b` to `b · t`. -/
public def symLine : SymmetricAlgebra R B →ₐ[R] MvPolynomial (Fin 1) B :=
  SymmetricAlgebra.lift (lineCoord R B)

/-- `symLine R B` sends `ι b` to `C b * X 0`. -/
@[simp] public theorem symLine_ι (b : B) :
    symLine R B (SymmetricAlgebra.ι R B b) =
      MvPolynomial.C b * MvPolynomial.X (0 : Fin 1) := by
  rw [symLine, SymmetricAlgebra.lift_ι_apply, lineCoord_apply]

/-- The homomorphism raises the degree-`d` part of `Sym_R(B)` into the degree-`d` part of
`B[t]`. -/
public theorem symLine_mem (d : ℕ) {x : SymmetricAlgebra R B}
    (hx : x ∈ SymPow.symmetricPower d R B) :
    symLine R B x ∈ polyGrading B 0 d := by
  rw [SymmetricAlgebra.symmetricPower_eq_span_prod_ι] at hx
  induction hx using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem y hy =>
      obtain ⟨s, rfl⟩ := hy
      rw [map_prod]
      have hfac : ∀ i : Fin d, symLine R B (SymmetricAlgebra.ι R B (s i)) =
          MvPolynomial.C (s i) * MvPolynomial.X (0 : Fin 1) := fun i => symLine_ι R B (s i)
      rw [Finset.prod_congr rfl fun i _ => hfac i, Finset.prod_mul_distrib,
        Finset.prod_const, ← map_prod, Finset.card_univ, Fintype.card_fin]
      have hgr := SetLike.mul_mem_graded
        ((MvPolynomial.mem_homogeneousSubmodule (σ := Fin (0 + 1)) 0
          (MvPolynomial.C (∏ x, s x))).2 (MvPolynomial.isHomogeneous_C _ _))
        (SetLike.pow_mem_graded d (X_mem_one B 0 0))
      simpa using hgr
  | zero => simp
  | add y z _ _ ihy ihz => rw [map_add]; exact add_mem ihy ihz
  | smul r y _ ih =>
      rw [Algebra.smul_def, map_mul, AlgHom.commutes]
      have hzero : (algebraMap R (MvPolynomial (Fin 1) B)) r ∈ polyGrading B 0 0 := by
        rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply R B (MvPolynomial (Fin 1) B),
          MvPolynomial.algebraMap_eq]
        exact (MvPolynomial.mem_homogeneousSubmodule _ _).2 (MvPolynomial.isHomogeneous_C _ _)
      simpa using SetLike.mul_mem_graded hzero ih

/-- **`Sym_R(B) ⟶ B[t]` as a homomorphism of graded rings.** -/
public def symLineGradedHom :
    (fun d : ℕ => SymPow.symmetricPower d R B) →+*ᵍ polyGrading B 0 where
  toRingHom := (symLine R B).toRingHom
  map_mem {d _} hx := symLine_mem R B d hx

/-- The underlying map of `symLineGradedHom R B` is `symLine R B`. -/
@[simp] public theorem symLineGradedHom_apply (x : SymmetricAlgebra R B) :
    symLineGradedHom R B x = symLine R B x := rfl

/-- **The degree-`d` component is surjective for every `d ≥ 1`**: the homogeneous element
`b · tᵈ` is the image of `b · 1^{d-1}`. -/
public theorem surjective_symLineGradedHom {d : ℕ} (hd : 1 ≤ d) :
    Function.Surjective (GradedRingHom.gradedAddHom (symLineGradedHom R B) d) := by
  obtain ⟨e, rfl⟩ := Nat.exists_eq_add_of_le hd
  have hι : ∀ b : B, SymmetricAlgebra.ι R B b ∈ SymPow.symmetricPower 1 R B := fun b => by
    rw [SymPow.symmetricPower, pow_one]
    exact LinearMap.mem_range_self _ b
  rintro ⟨y, hy⟩
  refine ⟨⟨SymmetricAlgebra.ι R B (y.coeff (Finsupp.single 0 (1 + e))) *
    SymmetricAlgebra.ι R B 1 ^ e, ?_⟩, ?_⟩
  · simpa using SetLike.mul_mem_graded (hι _) (SetLike.pow_mem_graded e (hι 1))
  · refine Subtype.ext ?_
    rw [GradedRingHom.gradedAddHom_apply_coe, symLineGradedHom_apply, map_mul, map_pow,
      symLine_ι, symLine_ι, map_one, one_mul, mul_assoc, ← pow_succ', Nat.add_comm e 1]
    exact (eq_C_mul_X_pow B hy).symm

/-- Eventual surjectivity, in the shape Tag 01N1 consumes. -/
public theorem eventually_surjective_symLineGradedHom :
    ∀ᶠ d : ℕ in Filter.atTop,
      Function.Surjective (GradedRingHom.gradedAddHom (symLineGradedHom R B) d) :=
  Filter.eventually_atTop.2 ⟨1, fun _ hd => surjective_symLineGradedHom R B hd⟩

/-! ### The closed immersion of projective spectra -/

/-- The morphism induced by `Sym_R(B) ⟶ B[t]` is defined on the whole of `Proj B[t]`. -/
public theorem mapDomain_symLineGradedHom_eq_top :
    mapDomain (fun d : ℕ => SymPow.symmetricPower d R B) (polyGrading B 0)
      (symLineGradedHom R B) = ⊤ :=
  Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjChain.mapDomain_eq_top_of_eventually_surjective _ _ _
    (eventually_surjective_symLineGradedHom R B)

/-- **The morphism `Proj B[t] ⟶ Proj (Sym_R B)`** induced by `Sym_R(B) ⟶ B[t]`. -/
public def projLineHom :
    AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (polyGrading B 0) ⟶
      AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (fun d : ℕ => SymPow.symmetricPower d R B) :=
  Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj.mapHomOfTop _ _ (symLineGradedHom R B)
    (mapDomain_symLineGradedHom_eq_top R B)

/-- **`Proj B[t] ⟶ Proj (Sym_R B)` is a closed immersion.** This is Tag 01N1 part (2) applied to
a homomorphism which is surjective in every positive degree. -/
public theorem isClosedImmersion_projLineHom : IsClosedImmersion (projLineHom R B) :=
  Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.SegreClosedImmersion.isClosedImmersion_mapHomOfTop _ _
    (symLineGradedHom R B) (mapDomain_symLineGradedHom_eq_top R B)
    (eventually_surjective_symLineGradedHom R B)

/-! ### `Proj B[t]` is `Spec B` -/

/-- The degree-zero homogeneous localization of `B[t]` at `t` is `B`: the standard chart of a
polynomial ring in one variable is the polynomial ring on no variables. -/
public def awayEquiv :
    HomogeneousLocalization.Away (polyGrading B 0) (MvPolynomial.X (0 : Fin 1)) ≃+* B :=
  letI : IsEmpty {j : Fin (0 + 1) // j ≠ 0} := ⟨fun j => j.2 (Fin.fin_one_eq_zero j.1)⟩
  (chartEquiv B 0 0).symm.trans (MvPolynomial.isEmptyRingEquiv B {j : Fin (0 + 1) // j ≠ 0})

/-- **The standard open of `t` is all of `Proj B[t]`.** Every homogeneous element of positive
degree is a multiple of a power of `t`, so a relevant homogeneous prime cannot contain `t`. -/
public theorem basicOpen_X_eq_top :
    AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen (polyGrading B 0) (MvPolynomial.X (0 : Fin 1)) = ⊤ := by
  refine top_le_iff.mp fun x _ => ?_
  rw [AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.mem_basicOpen]
  intro hx
  obtain ⟨n, f, hn, hf, hfx⟩ := exists_homogeneous_pos_notMem (polyGrading B 0) x
  refine hfx ?_
  rw [← HomogeneousIdeal.mem_iff] at hx ⊢
  rw [eq_C_mul_X_pow B hf]
  exact Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (Ideal.pow_mem_of_mem _ hx n hn)

/-- **`Proj B[t] ≅ Spec B`**: the standard open of `t` exhausts `Proj B[t]` and its degree-zero
homogeneous localization is `B`. -/
public def projIsoSpec :
    AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (polyGrading B 0) ≅ Spec (CommRingCat.of B) :=
  haveI : IsIso (CommRingCat.ofHom (awayEquiv B).symm.toRingHom) :=
    ((awayEquiv B).symm.toCommRingCatIso).isIso_hom
  (Scheme.topIso _).symm ≪≫
    (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (polyGrading B 0)).isoOfEq (basicOpen_X_eq_top B).symm ≪≫
      AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpenIsoSpec (polyGrading B 0) (MvPolynomial.X (0 : Fin 1))
        (X_mem_one B 0 0) Nat.one_pos ≪≫
      asIso (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (awayEquiv B).symm.toRingHom))

/-- **The morphism `Spec B ⟶ Proj (Sym_R B)`** cutting out `B` inside the projective spectrum of
its symmetric algebra. -/
public def specToProjSym :
    Spec (CommRingCat.of B) ⟶
      AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (fun d : ℕ => SymPow.symmetricPower d R B) :=
  (projIsoSpec B).inv ≫ projLineHom R B

/-- **An algebra is a closed subscheme of the `Proj` of its symmetric algebra**: the morphism
`Spec B ⟶ Proj (Sym_R B)` is a closed immersion. No finiteness of `B` over `R` and no hypothesis
on `R` is needed. -/
public theorem isClosedImmersion_specToProjSym : IsClosedImmersion (specToProjSym R B) := by
  have := isClosedImmersion_projLineHom R B
  rw [specToProjSym]
  infer_instance

end Stacks.SymAlgebraProjImmersion

end
